# UI overlay primitives

In `apps/web`, all modal and overlay UI must come from `@repo/ui`.

## Approved components

| Use case | Component | Import |
|----------|-----------|--------|
| Centered dialogs (confirm, forms, previews) | `Modal` | `@repo/ui` |
| Slide-over panels (mobile nav drawer) | `Sheet` | `@repo/ui` |
| Right-side detail panel (global third rail) | `ThirdRailProvider`, `ThirdRailHost`, `useThirdRail` | `@repo/ui` |
| Image select, crop, upload, expand | `PhotoUpload` | `@repo/ui` |

Storybook reference: `Components/Modal`, `Components/PhotoUpload`.

## Do not

- Use `createPortal` from `react-dom` in app code
- Add `aria-modal` on raw JSX elements
- Import `@radix-ui/react-dialog`, `@headlessui/react`, or similar overlay libraries
- Build custom fixed/backdrop/dialog markup in `apps/web`

ESLint enforces this via `@repo/eslint-config/ui-overlays` (wired in `apps/web/eslint.config.js`).

## When adding a new overlay

1. Check if `Modal` or `Sheet` fits the UX
2. If reusable across apps, add or extend a composite in `packages/ui/src/`
3. Keep low-level dialog wrappers internal to `@repo/ui` (not exported from the package root)
